From 34976f12161b88b8cba736c033b2211488bfb5b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 08:14:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] rdna-boosts: block 06: host-buffer revert for discrete
 GPUs

On the 050dde50c baseline this block reverted PR #24233 (restore
prop.integrated on HIP builds): integrated=true enables the CUDA host-buffer
path (zero-copy UMA weights) on APUs, which corrupts full-model results under
async execution on this box (PPL 5.9243 -> 8.51+ without HIP_LAUNCH_BLOCKING).

Re-based 2026-09-08 onto master 9113cc188: upstream itself reverted #24233 in
#28604 (2026-09-08), making forced-integrated-false the upstream default.  The
functional delta of this block is therefore now upstream; the block is retained
so the fork keeps its 14-block structure and carries only the rationale marker
comment above the (now unconditional) integrated = false line, guarding against
re-landing prop.integrated without re-testing this box.

Amended 2026-09-18 with the FA instance build fix: the MMA template instances are generated
per (ncols1, ncols2, head size) instead of per (ncols1, ncols2), and the head-512 instances are
listed first in the backend source order so they are not the tail of the build.  Build-time only:
identical explicit instantiations, identical symbols.  Also mirrors the ordering in the CUDA
backend's CMakeLists.txt.
